WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.500
we were very conscious to try and create

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.600
a different and even better experience for this movie in IMAX.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.860
it's unbelievably immersive, you know, incredible sound.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.620
and the image is second to none.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.760
You don't watch it you experience it.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.400
1917 is meant to be an immersive film

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.200
it's meant to feel like 115 minutes in someone else's life.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.120
and you want to see that on the biggest screen with the best sound system

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:32.940
it's a huge movie.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.000
It's very intimate it's very character driven

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.840
but the landscape it goes through is fast and stunning

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.360
what Roger Deakins achieved in this is unlike anything I've ever seen before.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.480
It's something special

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:51.340
The sort of power of it when it's played out over this sort of landscape

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:56.020
that IMAX can provide is even greater than a conventional movie theatre.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:01.760
you're not just seeing the letterbox version of the film. It gives you more space  at the top and bottom of the frame.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.100
so you feel more connected to the central characters.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.420
you just feel the walls of the trenches so close, closing in on you

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.980
you know what that extra little bit of space the IMAX screen affords you

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.060
that locks you into the story of these two men.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.920
Sam honest to god is a genius

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.640
he really is and to have a director that has such a crystal-clear vision

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.260
of the characters the story he's trying to tell

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.340
is very comforting. He's a very "actor's director".

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:40.380
1917 is kind of a bunch of A list cinema makers at the top of their games giving 110% everyday.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.460
The triumph of human spirit is what I hope they leave with.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:51.020
The reason to go and see it in the IMAX and go in the front row is that you're not going to watch a movie you're going to live one

